@startuml registration_flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Inter, Segoe UI, sans-serif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam shadowout false

skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    BorderColor #64748B
    FontColor #0F172A
    FontSize 11
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontSize 10
}

skinparam activityDiamond {
    BackgroundColor #FEF3C7
    BorderColor #D97706
    FontColor #92400E
}

title **Modern Laravel Blog - User Registration & Account Setup Flow**

|#EFF6FF|User (Browser / Client)|
|#F0FDF4|RegisteredUserController|
|#FAF5FF|SQLite Database (Users, Sessions)|

|User (Browser / Client)|
start
:User navigates to **GET /register**;

|RegisteredUserController|
:Render registration view (**<x-guest-layout>**);

|User (Browser / Client)|
:Fill in registration fields:
- Name
- Username (unique handle)
- Email (unique address)
- Password & Confirmation;
:Submit registration form via **POST /register**;

|RegisteredUserController|
:Validate inputs via standard rules:
- **name**: required | string | max:255
- **username**: required | alpha_dash | max:255 | unique:users
- **email**: required | string | lowercase | email | max:255 | unique:users
- **password**: required | string | confirmed | min:8;

if (Validation Rules Passed?) then (no - Errors Found)
    |User (Browser / Client)|
    :Return back to register view with:\n- Form error messages ($errors)\n- Preserved old input values; <<#FEE2E2>>
    stop
else (yes - Valid)
    |RegisteredUserController|
    :Hash password via **Hash::make($password)**;

    |SQLite Database (Users, Sessions)|
    :Execute **User::create([...])**;
    :Set default avatar using seed:\n""api.dicebear.com/7.x/avataaars/svg?seed={username}"";
    :Insert new user record into **users** table;

    |RegisteredUserController|
    :Trigger Laravel **Registered** event;
    :Authenticate newly created user via **Auth::login($user)**;
    :$request->session()->regenerate();

    |SQLite Database (Users, Sessions)|
    :Record new active session in **sessions** table;

    |User (Browser / Client)|
    :Redirect to **/dashboard** with active session\n(Logged in as author); <<#DCFCE7>>
    stop
endif

@enduml
